IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc2-explosives.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II, ss 79 to 82.1 ("Dangerous Materials and Devices", explosives): the duty of care re explosives, breach of duty,
-- using explosives, possession of an explosive, and the consecutive-sentence rule of s 82.1. Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a
-- converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) / NOTHING (not covered): see the header of ccc2-treason.l4 and NOTES.md.
-- "explosive substance" is s 2's term ("includes ..."): its answer is a seam input `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` (a MAYBE BOOLEAN).

§ `Section 79 -- Duty of care re explosive`

-- "Every one who has an explosive substance in his possession or under his care or control is under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent bodily harm or death to persons or damage to property
-- by that explosive substance."
-- src:1190 | Duty of care re explosive
-- src:1191 | 79 Every one who has an explosive substance in his possession or under his care or control is under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent bodily harm or death to persons or damage to property by that explosive substance.
@ref Criminal Code s 79 (duty of care re explosive) (src:1190-1191)
GIVEN `the person has the thing in their possession or under their care or control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79 the person is under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by the explosive substance` MEANS
    IF `the person has the thing in their possession or under their care or control` AND `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who has an explosive substance in his possession or under his care or control" (s 2 "explosive substance includes" leaves other things open)

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the text states no time, so no WITHIN is invented; the duty stands while the person has the thing.
@ref Criminal Code s 79 (duty of care re explosive) (src:1190-1191)
DECLARE `s 79 act` IS ONE OF `s 79 uses reasonable care to prevent bodily harm or death to persons or damage to property by the explosive substance`

@ref Criminal Code s 79 (duty of care re explosive) (src:1190-1191)
`s 79 the duty of care` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 79 uses reasonable care to prevent bodily harm or death to persons or damage to property by the explosive substance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 79: the person did not use reasonable care to prevent bodily harm or death to persons or damage to property by the explosive substance"

§ `Section 80 -- Breach of duty`

-- "Every one who, being under a legal duty within the meaning of section 79, fails without lawful excuse to perform that duty, is guilty of an indictable offence and, if as a result an explosion of an
-- explosive substance occurs that (a) causes death or is likely to cause death to any person, is liable to imprisonment for life; or (b) causes bodily harm or damage to property or is likely to cause bodily
-- harm or damage to property, is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years." The offence is made out by the failure; the penalty is stated only where an explosion results (seam: when it
-- does not, the penalty is that of the general provisions, which are outside this part, so the answer is NOTHING).
-- src:1192 | Breach of duty
-- src:1193 | 80 Every one who, being under a legal duty within the meaning of section 79, fails without lawful excuse to perform that duty, is guilty of an indictable offence and, if as a result an explosion of an explosive substance occurs that
-- src:1194 | (a) causes death or is likely to cause death to any person, is liable to imprisonment for life; or
-- src:1195 | (b) causes bodily harm or damage to property or is likely to cause bodily harm or damage to property, is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 80 (breach of duty) (src:1192-1195)
GIVEN `s 79 the person is under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by the explosive substance: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to perform that duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80 the person commits the offence of breach of duty` MEANS
    IF `s 79 the person is under a legal duty to use reasonable care to prevent harm by the explosive substance: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person fails to perform that duty` AND (NOT `the person has a lawful excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "being under a legal duty within the meaning of section 79, fails without lawful excuse to perform that duty"

@ref Criminal Code s 80 (breach of duty) (src:1192-1195)
`s 80 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 80 (breach of duty) (src:1192-1195)
DECLARE `s 80 result` IS ONE OF
    `s 80(a) an explosion occurs as a result that causes death or is likely to cause death to any person`
    `s 80(b) an explosion occurs as a result that causes bodily harm or damage to property or is likely to cause bodily harm or damage to property`
    `s 80 no explosion occurs as a result`

@ref Criminal Code s 80 (breach of duty) (src:1192-1195)
GIVEN result IS A `s 80 result`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 80 the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER result
    WHEN `s 80(a) an explosion occurs as a result that causes death or is likely to cause death to any person` THEN JUST (LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `s 80(b) an explosion occurs as a result that causes bodily harm or damage to property or is likely to cause bodily harm or damage to property` THEN JUST (LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `s 80 no explosion occurs as a result` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states a penalty only "if as a result an explosion of an explosive substance occurs"

§ `Section 81 -- Using explosives`

-- Subsection (1): "Every one commits an offence who (a) does anything with intent to cause an explosion of an explosive substance that is likely to cause serious bodily harm or death to persons or is likely to
-- cause serious damage to property; (b) with intent to do bodily harm to any person (i) causes an explosive substance to explode, (ii) sends or delivers to a person or causes a person to take or receive an
-- explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing, or (iii) places or throws anywhere or at or on a person a corrosive fluid, explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing;
-- (c) with intent to destroy or damage property without lawful excuse, places or throws an explosive substance anywhere; or (d) makes or has in his possession or has under his care or control any explosive
-- substance with intent thereby (i) to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property, or (ii) to enable another person to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property."
-- src:1196 | Using explosives
-- src:1197 | 81 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:1198 | (a) does anything with intent to cause an explosion of an explosive substance that is likely to cause serious bodily harm or death to persons or is likely to cause serious damage to property;
-- src:1199 | (b) with intent to do bodily harm to any person
-- src:1200 | (i) causes an explosive substance to explode,
-- src:1201 | (ii) sends or delivers to a person or causes a person to take or receive an explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing, or
-- src:1202 | (iii) places or throws anywhere or at or on a person a corrosive fluid, explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing;
-- src:1203 | (c) with intent to destroy or damage property without lawful excuse, places or throws an explosive substance anywhere; or
-- src:1204 | (d) makes or has in his possession or has under his care or control any explosive substance with intent thereby
-- src:1205 | (i) to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property, or
-- src:1206 | (ii) to enable another person to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property.
@ref Criminal Code s 81(1) (using explosives) (src:1196-1206)
DECLARE `s 81(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 81(1)(a) does anything with intent to cause an explosion of an explosive substance that is likely to cause serious bodily harm or death to persons or is likely to cause serious damage to property`
    `s 81(1)(b)(i) with intent to do bodily harm to any person, causes an explosive substance to explode`
    `s 81(1)(b)(ii) with intent to do bodily harm to any person, sends or delivers to a person or causes a person to take or receive an explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing`
    `s 81(1)(b)(iii) with intent to do bodily harm to any person, places or throws anywhere or at or on a person a corrosive fluid, explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing`
    `s 81(1)(c) with intent to destroy or damage property without lawful excuse, places or throws an explosive substance anywhere`
    `s 81(1)(d)(i) makes or has in his possession or has under his care or control any explosive substance with intent thereby to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property`
    `s 81(1)(d)(ii) makes or has in his possession or has under his care or control any explosive substance with intent thereby to enable another person to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property`
    `s 81(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (d)`

@ref Criminal Code s 81(1) (using explosives) (src:1196-1206)
GIVEN act IS A `s 81(1) act`
      `the person has the intent the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the explosion is likely to cause serious bodily harm or death to persons or is likely to cause serious damage to property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a corrosive fluid, or any other dangerous substance or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) the person commits an offence by using explosives` MEANS
    IF act EQUALS `s 81(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (d)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one commits an offence who (a) ... (d)"
    ELSE IF `its paragraph is met`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph's own conditions ("with intent", "explosive substance", "without lawful excuse")
    WHERE
        `the thing is an explosive substance` MEANS `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `its paragraph is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER act
            WHEN `s 81(1)(a) does anything with intent to cause an explosion of an explosive substance that is likely to cause serious bodily harm or death to persons or is likely to cause serious damage to property` THEN `the person has the intent the paragraph names` AND `the explosion is likely to cause serious bodily harm or death to persons or is likely to cause serious damage to property` AND `the thing is an explosive substance`
            WHEN `s 81(1)(b)(i) with intent to do bodily harm to any person, causes an explosive substance to explode` THEN `the person has the intent the paragraph names` AND `the thing is an explosive substance`
            WHEN `s 81(1)(b)(ii) with intent to do bodily harm to any person, sends or delivers to a person or causes a person to take or receive an explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing` THEN `the person has the intent the paragraph names` AND (`the thing is an explosive substance` OR `the thing is a corrosive fluid, or any other dangerous substance or thing`)
            WHEN `s 81(1)(b)(iii) with intent to do bodily harm to any person, places or throws anywhere or at or on a person a corrosive fluid, explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing` THEN `the person has the intent the paragraph names` AND (`the thing is an explosive substance` OR `the thing is a corrosive fluid, or any other dangerous substance or thing`)
            WHEN `s 81(1)(c) with intent to destroy or damage property without lawful excuse, places or throws an explosive substance anywhere` THEN `the person has the intent the paragraph names` AND `the person acts without lawful excuse` AND `the thing is an explosive substance`
            WHEN `s 81(1)(d)(i) makes or has in his possession or has under his care or control any explosive substance with intent thereby to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property` THEN `the person has the intent the paragraph names` AND `the thing is an explosive substance`
            WHEN `s 81(1)(d)(ii) makes or has in his possession or has under his care or control any explosive substance with intent thereby to enable another person to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property` THEN `the person has the intent the paragraph names` AND `the thing is an explosive substance`
            WHEN `s 81(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (d)` THEN FALSE

-- Subsection (2): "Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable (a) for an offence under paragraph (1)(a) or (b), to imprisonment for life; or
-- (b) for an offence under paragraph (1)(c) or (d), to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years."
-- src:1207 | Punishment
-- src:1208 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:1209 | (a) for an offence under paragraph (1)(a) or (b), to imprisonment for life; or
-- src:1210 | (b) for an offence under paragraph (1)(c) or (d), to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 81(2) (punishment) (src:1207-1210)
`s 81(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 81(2) (punishment) (src:1207-1210)
GIVEN act IS A `s 81(1) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 81(2) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 81(1)(a) does anything with intent to cause an explosion of an explosive substance that is likely to cause serious bodily harm or death to persons or is likely to cause serious damage to property` THEN JUST (LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `s 81(1)(b)(i) with intent to do bodily harm to any person, causes an explosive substance to explode` THEN JUST (LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `s 81(1)(b)(ii) with intent to do bodily harm to any person, sends or delivers to a person or causes a person to take or receive an explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing` THEN JUST (LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `s 81(1)(b)(iii) with intent to do bodily harm to any person, places or throws anywhere or at or on a person a corrosive fluid, explosive substance or any other dangerous substance or thing` THEN JUST (LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `s 81(1)(c) with intent to destroy or damage property without lawful excuse, places or throws an explosive substance anywhere` THEN JUST (LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `s 81(1)(d)(i) makes or has in his possession or has under his care or control any explosive substance with intent thereby to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property` THEN JUST (LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `s 81(1)(d)(ii) makes or has in his possession or has under his care or control any explosive substance with intent thereby to enable another person to endanger life or to cause serious damage to property` THEN JUST (LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN `s 81(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (d)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) states a punishment only for an offence under a paragraph of subsection (1)

§ `Sections 82 and 82.1 -- Possession of explosive; sentences to be served consecutively`

-- Subsection (1): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, makes or has in their possession or under their care or control any explosive substance is guilty of (a) an indictable offence and liable to
-- imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction."
-- src:1211 | Possession of explosive
-- src:1212 | 82 (1) Every person who, without lawful excuse, makes or has in their possession or under their care or control any explosive substance is guilty of
-- src:1213 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:1214 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 82(1) (possession of explosive) (src:1211-1214)
GIVEN `the person makes, or has in their possession or under their care or control, the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(1) the person possesses an explosive substance without lawful excuse` MEANS
    IF `the person makes, or has in their possession or under their care or control, the thing` AND `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (NOT `the person has a lawful excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, makes or has in their possession or under their care or control any explosive substance"

@ref Criminal Code s 82(1) (punishment) (src:1211-1214)
`s 82(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 82(1) (punishment) (src:1211-1214)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 82(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- Subsection (2): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, makes or has in their possession or under their care or control any explosive substance for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association
-- with a criminal organization is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years." "Criminal organization" is s 2's term (a seam input).
-- src:1215 | Possession in association with criminal organization
-- src:1216 | (2) Every person who, without lawful excuse, makes or has in their possession or under their care or control any explosive substance for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref Criminal Code s 82(2) (possession in association with criminal organization) (src:1215-1216)
GIVEN `the person makes, or has in their possession or under their care or control, the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 criminal organization: the group is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(2) the person possesses an explosive substance for or with a criminal organization` MEANS
    IF `the person makes, or has in their possession or under their care or control, the thing` AND `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (NOT `the person has a lawful excuse`)
        AND `the thing is for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a group` AND `s 2 criminal organization: the group is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization"

@ref Criminal Code s 82(2) (punishment) (src:1215-1216)
`s 82(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 82(2) (punishment) (src:1215-1216)
`s 82(2) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- Section 82.1: "A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection 82(2) shall be served consecutively to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or
-- series of events and to any other sentence to which the person is subject at the time the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under subsection 82(2)."
-- src:1217 | Sentences to be served consecutively
-- src:1218 | 82.1 A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection 82(2) shall be served consecutively to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events and to any other sentence to which the person is subject at the time the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under subsection 82(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 82.1 (sentences to be served consecutively) (src:1217-1218)
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection 82(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other punishment is imposed for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to the other sentence at the time the sentence is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82.1 the sentence must be served consecutively to the other punishment or sentence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection 82(2)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection 82(2)"
        IF `the other punishment is imposed for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` OR `the person is subject to the other sentence at the time the sentence is imposed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any other punishment ... for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events and to any other sentence to which the person is subject at the time"
